1. Removed Jest-specific mocking (`jest.mock`) since we're in a browser environment, not a test environment
2. Created proper React component mocks instead of Jest mocks
3. Added a basic Providers wrapper component to handle any potential context requirements
4. Added mock utilities as regular objects/functions
5. Added the mock modules to the window object to make them globally available
6. Kept the core component structure but wrapped it in the Providers component

This should resolve the module fetching error by providing the necessary mock implementations in a way that works in the browser environment. If you still see any specific errors related to missing dependencies or contexts, please let me know and I can help adjust the mocking strategy further.

